{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "faa1fe57-3dd8-5136-93c3-fe9bdbeccd4d",
  "Description": "40 balls fall into a pile, and a volume built from their positions wraps them in one skin.\n\nThe other direction: physics feeding a volume. [ReadPointsFromGpu] reads the poses of [PhysicsWorld] back every frame, [VolumeFromPoints] splats them into a density volume and [VolumeToMesh] extracts a surface from it.\n\nAKA: metaballs, blob, skin, liquid, points to volume, surface\n\nTips\n- This rebuilds a volume and a mesh every frame on the CPU. Keep the body count low and VoxelSize coarse.\n- Isovalue on [VolumeToMesh] is the density at which the skin sits: lower is fatter.\n- Radius on [VolumeFromPoints] should be larger than the ball radius so neighbouring balls merge.",
  "InputUis": [],
